flowchart TD
    User[Authenticated user selects due window]
    User --> Query[GET calibrations due with required within_days]
    Query --> DueCheck{next_calibration_due before today?}
    DueCheck -->|Yes| Overdue[Return OVERDUE status and passport warning]
    DueCheck -->|No, within requested window| Upcoming[Return UPCOMING status]
    DueCheck -->|Outside requested window| Omit[Do not include in due response]

    Technician[ULMD_ADMIN or MAINTENANCE_TECH] --> SelectAsset[Select asset and enter calibration details]
    SelectAsset --> Validate{Category requires calibration and has positive interval?}
    Validate -->|No| Reject[Reject request with conflict]
    Validate -->|Yes| Calculate[Calculate next_due_date from calibration date plus category interval]
    Calculate --> Save[Append calibration_logs record]
    Save --> Passed{Calibration passed?}
    Passed -->|Yes| UpdatePass[Update asset last_calibrated_date and next_calibration_due]
    Passed -->|No| UpdateFail[Update last_calibrated_date only; retain prior asset due date]
    UpdatePass --> Audit[Append calibration and asset snapshots to audit_logs in same transaction]
    UpdateFail --> Audit
    Audit --> History[Retain record in calibration history]

    %% Reminder window is supplied by the caller. No scheduler or notification is implemented.
    %% Failed-calibration asset disposition requires stakeholder approval (DEC-13).
